        "hypothesis": "__AUTH_HEADERS__ is not a mapping in TestSprite's V3 sandbox (most likely a JSON string).",
        "mechanism": "Every authenticated helper does `headers.update(__AUTH_HEADERS__)` (MCP) or `dict(__AUTH_HEADERS__)` (middleware). Both raise ValueError/TypeError on a str. The exception is thrown before any request leaves the sandbox, which is why the middleware side is reported as 'blocked' rather than 'failed' - the runner never got to an assertion.",
